---
import SectionHead from '../SectionHead.astro';
import Logo from '../Logo.astro';
---

<section class="section" id="how-it-decides" aria-labelledby="feature-title" data-signal="explain">
  <div class="container grid-12 feature">
    <div class="feature-text" data-slide="left">
      <SectionHead name="Reasons" />
      <h2 id="feature-title" class="h-section">Every change comes <span class="accent">with a reason.</span></h2>
      <div class="collapsible long">
        <p class="clip">
          A page that changes without telling anyone is a page nobody can trust. So every change Shapewell makes is listed in
          plain language, with the numbers behind it: how long you rested on a section, how fast you scrolled, which
          button you pressed. Your team sees the same list in the studio, so a surprising change is never a mystery.
        </p>
        <button type="button" class="more-btn" aria-expanded="false">Read more</button>
      </div>
      <div class="expand-researcher explain-more">
        <p class="label label-sm"><span class="c">How the scoring works</span></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Signals are sampled every 250 ms and kept in memory.</li>
          <li>After the first 8 seconds, three profiles are scored every 2 seconds.</li>
          <li>The top profile wins only if it leads the next by at least 25 %. Otherwise the page stays default.</li>
          <li>A new shape holds for at least 20 seconds, so the page never flickers.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-open-studio aria-controls="studio" aria-expanded="false">See your own reasons</button>
    </div>

    <div class="mock" data-slide="right" aria-label="Example of the studio's Why this changed list" role="img">
      <div class="mock-head">
        <Logo size={22} wordmark={false} href={null} />
        <span class="label label-sm"><span class="c">Why this changed</span> / example</span>
      </div>
      <ul class="mock-list" aria-hidden="true">
        <li><span class="mono">Signal</span>You rested on the code block for 3.4 s, so install moved up.</li>
        <li><span class="mono">Signal</span>You scroll fast (about 1,900 px/s), so long paragraphs were shortened.</li>
        <li><span class="mono">Layout</span>Spacing tightened to a compact density.</li>
        <li><span class="mono">Copy</span>Main button now says "Copy the snippet".</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="mock-foot mono">Builder 6.8 · Buyer 1.2 · Researcher 2.0</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .feature {
    align-items: start;
    row-gap: 40px;
  }
  .feature-text {
    grid-column: 1 / span 6;
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    justify-items: start;
  }
  .feature-text .section-head {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .collapsible p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .explain-more ul {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .explain-more li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .mock {
    grid-column: 8 / span 5;
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .mock-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .mock-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 6px 18px;
  }
  .mock-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 64px 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .mock-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .mock-list .mono {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--cobalt);
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .mock-foot {
    padding: 12px 18px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    color: var(--slate);
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .feature-text,
    .mock {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
</style>
